-- title:
--   Commutativity of the divisor correspondences α_*β^* at two primes
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N \ge 1$ and primes $\ell$, $\ell'$, $q'$ with $\ell \ne q'$, $\ell' \ne q'$ and $q' \nmid N$ (no constraint relates $\ell$ and $\ell'$: they may coincide and may divide $N$), and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q'$. Inside $k((q))$ consider the intermediate field $F_N :=$ `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, the $k$-subextension generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k N`, and, for a prime $q$, the roof `charLDegeneracyRoof k N q`, the $k$-subextension generated by `jqModC k`, `jqNModC k N`, `jqNModC k q` and `jqNModC k (N * q)`; thus $F_N = k(j(q), j(q^N))$ and the roof is $k(j(q), j(q^N), j(q^{q}), j(q^{Nq}))$. Assume both roofs, at $\ell$ and at $\ell'$, have principal divisors, i.e. each nonzero element has an associated divisor recording its orders at all places and of degree $0$. Assume further that the two legs $\alpha$ (`heckeAlphaC`, the inclusion of $F_N$ into the roof) and $\beta$ (`heckeBetaC`, the leg induced by the $q$-expansion substitution) are integral ring maps, at $\ell$ and at $\ell'$. Then for every divisor $D$ of $F_N$ over $k$ (a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the places of $F_N/k$), the two operators $\mathcal{T}_q := \alpha_* \circ \beta^*$, pull-back along $\beta$ followed by push-forward along $\alpha$, for $q = \ell$ and $q = \ell'$, satisfy $\mathcal{T}_\ell(\mathcal{T}_{\ell'}(D)) = \mathcal{T}_{\ell'}(\mathcal{T}_\ell(D))$.
--
--   This is the commutativity of the Hecke correspondences $T_\ell$ (or $U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$) acting on divisors of the modular curve of level $N$ over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q' \nmid N$, taken in the orientation $\alpha_*\beta^*$ that matches the modular rule $T_\ell(E,C) = \sum_D (E/D, (C+D)/D)$. It feeds the verification of the Hecke relations in [`ModularCurve.SSLevelDatum.heckeLaws_of_prime_ne_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSLevelDatum.heckeLaws_of_prime_ne_of_not_dvd).
